1
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,964
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

2
00:00:53,386 --> 00:00:56,056
God, she won't even pick up at all…

3
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:57,932
Y'think something's going on here?

4
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:00,477
No way. What could have possibly happened?

5
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:03,605
Oh, I swear to God…

6
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:06,816
Ugh, this is just unreal.

7
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:07,901
Hey, wait, don't… don't…

8
00:01:07,984 --> 00:01:10,195
Let's wait a little longer.
Comrade, come on.

9
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:13,073
My God, that girl, I swear I'm gonna…

10
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:14,157
EPISODE 9

11
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,159
How could she skip her own graduation?

12
00:01:16,242 --> 00:01:18,912
We've all been waiting for this day
for so long.

13
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:30,256
Yeah, yeah, we've waited
so long for this day.

14
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:34,761
Just wait till she gets back.
Then, it'll be on.

15
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:37,305
I'll give that girl a piece of my mind!

16
00:01:40,308 --> 00:01:43,103
- Oh, geez.
- Oh, good Lord.

17
00:01:43,978 --> 00:01:46,564
- Honestly, that little punk!
- Hey, comrade. Hey, hey, comrade, wait!

18
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:48,733
Hey, Su-jeong, get up! Su-jeong!

19
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:54,697
Good grief, you put down
some big plates, didn't you? Goodness.

20
00:02:00,745 --> 00:02:04,374
I was just gonna observe a surgery
for a bit before I went, but then…

21
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:05,458
Sorry, Miss Jang.

22
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:08,378
If you were watching,
then why is there blood on your face?

23
00:02:09,003 --> 00:02:11,881
Well, actually, they said I should
at least get to try a little,

24
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:14,634
you know, since I skipped graduation
to see the surgery.

25
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:16,886
So they called me over, and I had a look…

26
00:02:18,346 --> 00:02:19,556
I'm so sorry.

27
00:02:19,639 --> 00:02:21,683
Oh, my goodness. Oh me, oh my.

28
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:24,602
Whoa.

29
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:28,815
Wow! What is this, Eung-gu?
How'd you get something so rare?

30
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:32,861
It was your aunt.
To congratulate you, she hand-baked it.

31
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:35,780
Do you know how hard it is
to get white rice here in Cuba?

32
00:02:35,864 --> 00:02:37,240
- Nobody's got any.
- Wow.

33
00:02:38,283 --> 00:02:39,617
Ow!

34
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:44,622
Hey, Su-jeong. Kid, look at me and auntie.

35
00:02:44,706 --> 00:02:47,167
We got all dressed up to honor you.

36
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:49,544
This is a once-in-a-lifetime event.

37
00:02:51,171 --> 00:02:53,047
Hey, did you… Did you just laugh?

38
00:02:53,131 --> 00:02:54,883
You could've put this on at least.

39
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:58,011
And then let Auntie try it on
and then give me a turn on it too.

40
00:02:58,094 --> 00:03:01,806
And then we could've taken some pictures
with it, and be normal people for a day.

41
00:03:08,396 --> 00:03:09,522
I made a mistake.

42
00:03:12,317 --> 00:03:13,318
Man!

43
00:03:15,486 --> 00:03:19,532
Tsk. But then again,
who's the one who raised her this way?

44
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:21,743
Comrade Hui-suk, it was you.

45
00:03:21,826 --> 00:03:24,412
This is on you.

46
00:03:32,086 --> 00:03:33,713
Hey, you should make a wish.

47
00:03:44,515 --> 00:03:45,934
<i>Repeat after me.</i>

48
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:49,437
<i>"I, as a member of</i>
<i>the medical profession…"</i>

49
00:03:50,271 --> 00:03:54,525
<i>"I, as a member of</i>
<i>the medical profession…"</i>

50
00:03:55,151 --> 00:04:00,531
<i>"…solemnly pledge to dedicate</i>
<i>my life to the service of humanity."</i>

51
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:05,578
<i>"I solemnly pledge to dedicate</i>
<i>my life to the service of humanity."</i>

52
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:09,165
<i>"I will practice my profession</i>
<i>with conscience and dignity,</i>

53
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:11,709
<i>and in accordance</i>
<i>with good medical practice."</i>

54
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:14,003
<i>"I will give to my teachers,</i>
<i>colleagues and students,</i>

55
00:04:14,087 --> 00:04:16,422
<i>the respect and gratitude</i>
<i>that is their due."</i>

56
00:04:18,716 --> 00:04:22,428
"I'll treat the patient's health
as the sole highest priority

57
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:24,389
and handle it with the highest care."

58
00:04:24,472 --> 00:04:28,017
"I'll treat the patient's health
as the sole highest priority

59
00:04:28,101 --> 00:04:29,894
and handle it with the highest care."

60
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:35,275
"This day, I solemnly swear this oath,

61
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:37,735
taken freely and on my honor,

62
00:04:37,819 --> 00:04:41,948
to uphold these doctrines
as is our duty as long as I live."

63
00:04:45,243 --> 00:04:48,288
"This day, I solemnly swear this oath,

64
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:49,914
taken freely on my honor,

65
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:55,295
to uphold these doctrines
as is our duty as long as I live."

66
00:05:13,813 --> 00:05:16,482
Congrats, Gye Su-jeong,
you're a doctor now!

67
00:05:17,358 --> 00:05:18,568
Yeah!

68
00:05:20,278 --> 00:05:23,239
Miss Jang Hui-suk
is the reason I became a doctor.

69
00:05:24,032 --> 00:05:25,283
Thank you for everything.

70
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:27,952
I made it because of you.

71
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:38,046
Oh, hey, we should take a picture too.

72
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:40,590
Oh.

73
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:42,717
- Oh, there it is.
- Okay.

74
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:55,605
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

75
00:06:06,866 --> 00:06:08,076
Kocher maneuver.

76
00:06:09,327 --> 00:06:10,495
A SURGICAL TECHNIQUE
THAT SEPARATES THE DUODENUM

77
00:06:10,578 --> 00:06:11,662
AND PANCREATIC HEAD
FROM SURROUNDING TISSUE

78
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:15,166
I told Ms. Jae-seon to come,
just in case. She'll be here later.

79
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:24,592
<i>I can't help but wonder,</i>
<i>who is Gye Su-jeong exactly?</i>

80
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:26,719
Are Gye Su-jeong…

81
00:06:28,971 --> 00:06:31,808
and Doctor X the same person?

82
00:06:41,901 --> 00:06:43,486
Well, I applaud you.

83
00:06:44,612 --> 00:06:47,573
She is Doctor X. It's the same person.

84
00:06:49,784 --> 00:06:52,870
Ah, in that circumstance, well…

85
00:06:53,538 --> 00:06:56,040
In-In that circumstance,
the results of this operation--

86
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:58,584
If Doctor X is someone that
puts their patients' lives

87
00:06:58,668 --> 00:07:01,379
above all else in the world, then yes.

88
00:07:02,422 --> 00:07:04,632
Gye Su-jeong is Dr. X. Make no mistake.

89
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:08,010
If Dr. X is someone
who never leaves the patient's side,

90
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:11,722
and stands by them,
Gye Su-jeong is Dr. X, that's clear.

91
00:07:13,141 --> 00:07:16,936
If Dr. X is someone who gives their all
to the surgery entrusted to them,

92
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:20,523
then Gye Su-jeong is Dr. X. Absolutely.

93
00:07:20,606 --> 00:07:24,861
If Dr. X is what you call a doctor
who doesn't fail, then it's certain,

94
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:28,781
Gye Su-jeong would be Dr. X
more than anyone.

95
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:30,450
Ms. Jang, that is enough.

96
00:07:30,533 --> 00:07:32,493
What could you possibly stand to gain here

97
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:34,579
creating suspicion and paranoia
around a doctor

98
00:07:34,662 --> 00:07:37,957
who's treating patients at your hospital,
which is rapidly declining?

99
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:40,543
Just four weeks after the surgery
the patient fell dead.

100
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:45,047
Mr. Park Gwang-cheol is alive I might add.
And doing great in his recovery, Director.

101
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,097
Have you forgotten

102
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:57,101
who actually pulled the strings to secure
your snazzy new position here?

103
00:07:58,686 --> 00:08:00,396
<i>Even though you left, these stayed behind.</i>

104
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,856
THIS IS A STERILIZED PRODUCT
MAY CAUSE ALLERGIC REACTIONS

105
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:03,900
<i>So what I shared with you,</i>
<i>was it of good use to you?</i>

106
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:06,486
Then we'll settle that
some other occasion, Director.

107
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:11,991
Is this what you're expecting to get
in return for that?

108
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:15,453
That's the trump card.

109
00:08:16,329 --> 00:08:20,917
I couldn't possibly waste my hand
on a careless unfounded rumor, could I?

110
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:23,586
On an unfounded rumor, huh?

111
00:08:25,004 --> 00:08:27,882
Now, if I were to start digging
into Dr. Gye Su-jeong's history…

112
00:08:27,965 --> 00:08:30,343
You're struggling with glaucoma,
aren't you?

113
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:34,555
It doesn't seem you've lost
your sight completely.

114
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:37,350
Why didn't you handle Yeo Jeong-sun's
surgery then, Director?

115
00:08:41,103 --> 00:08:44,899
Ah. It's not that
your eyesight is closing in.

116
00:08:45,816 --> 00:08:48,528
It's that your macular vision
is going first.

117
00:08:49,862 --> 00:08:51,906
How does that pertain to this, Ms. Jang?

118
00:08:51,989 --> 00:08:56,118
Director, surely you must be
curious about how I found that out.

119
00:08:56,202 --> 00:08:57,787
I have to say I was curious myself.

120
00:08:57,870 --> 00:09:01,123
How is it that a surgeon
once labeled the hand of God

121
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:06,045
put down his precious scalpel to come
wrestle with everyone in the muddy swamp?

122
00:09:10,174 --> 00:09:12,843
You have too much time on your hands.

123
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:16,597
- Surely you have better things to do.
- Ms. Jang Hui-suk.

124
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:19,350
This is what you'd call…

125
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:22,019
poetic justice of
the highest order, Director.

126
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,566
Gye Su-jeong…

127
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:30,194
is Doctor X, beyond a shadow of a doubt.

128
00:09:32,613 --> 00:09:37,201
A doctor that takes risky cases for which
absolutely no surgical techniques exist.

129
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:42,248
Beginning hilum dissection.

130
00:09:42,331 --> 00:09:43,833
PROCESS OF DISSECTING AROUND THE
HILUM, THE GATEWAY THROUGH WHICH

131
00:09:43,916 --> 00:09:45,543
AN ORGAN'S BLOOD VESSELS, DUCTS,
AND OTHER STRUCTURES ENTER AND EXIT

132
00:09:45,626 --> 00:09:48,796
<i>Or an arrogant hand of God</i>
<i>who takes pleasure in weighing human life</i>

133
00:09:48,879 --> 00:09:51,299
<i>against the sharpness of her own skills.</i>

134
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:58,347
Ga-eul, hang in there
just a little longer.

135
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:06,314
<i>A name that carries with it</i>
<i>both respect and derision.</i>

136
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:14,989
You've already gotten that far?
I guess I didn't even need to come, huh?

137
00:10:15,072 --> 00:10:18,159
- Wow, things must've moved really fast.
- Why are you here?

138
00:10:18,242 --> 00:10:21,412
I came to assist,
and to observe Dr. Gye operate.

139
00:10:21,495 --> 00:10:23,289
He ran over here like crazy.

140
00:10:23,372 --> 00:10:24,957
When I tie it off, please hold it for me.

141
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,751
- Yes.
- I didn't mean you.

142
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:29,545
Oh, for sure. Ms. Jae-seon
is much better than me.

143
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:31,839
Posteroinferior coming up.

144
00:10:31,922 --> 00:10:35,217
- Already? No way.
- Not "no way." She really is that fast.

145
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:37,261
We need to identify and protect
the right ureter,

146
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:39,889
- so please page Urology now.
- Okay, will do.

147
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:46,312
<i>I think that is what the</i>
<i>name Doctor X truly stands to represent,</i>

148
00:10:46,395 --> 00:10:47,396
<i>and therefore…</i>

149
00:10:48,814 --> 00:10:50,524
<i>to me, Gye Su-jeong</i>

150
00:10:51,817 --> 00:10:53,903
is Doctor X,
there's no mistake about that.

151
00:10:58,699 --> 00:11:00,618
Son of a bitch.

152
00:11:05,456 --> 00:11:10,628
You're nothing, you're just director
at a branch facility of Guseo University.

153
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:15,758
Even if you've discovered who she is,
Doctor X's identity,

154
00:11:16,884 --> 00:11:19,178
you can't do a thing about it
with where you're at.

155
00:11:22,765 --> 00:11:25,267
She barely got herself out of there
and re-oriented.

156
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:29,021
And she's hanging by a thread.

157
00:11:29,772 --> 00:11:34,443
You're digging into the past of
someone who's trying so hard to save lives

158
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:35,528
and still…

159
00:11:36,195 --> 00:11:38,197
you lack the power to do anything.

160
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:55,089
I didn't think you'd do it all yourself

161
00:11:55,172 --> 00:11:56,966
without consulting other departments.

162
00:11:57,049 --> 00:11:58,592
If it's urgent, you have to.

163
00:11:58,676 --> 00:12:00,553
Dr. Gye is amazing, isn't she?

164
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:09,895
I'll do it, Dr. Gye.
At least let me do this so I feel less…

165
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:11,564
Shouldn't you get going?

166
00:12:11,647 --> 00:12:13,232
You finished so quickly
that I have some time to spare.

167
00:12:13,315 --> 00:12:14,525
SURGERY TIME - CURRENT TIME
ANESTHESIA TIME

168
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:17,194
You have 40 minutes
until you get off work, Dr. Gye.

169
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:19,572
And I have 40 minutes
until my next surgery.

170
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:22,783
I have some time to spare myself.

171
00:12:25,453 --> 00:12:30,124
Uh, Dr. Gye also needs to do this
for herself. So don't worry about it.

172
00:12:42,762 --> 00:12:45,681
Dr. Gye Su-jeong, great work as always.

173
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:47,183
Great work, Doctor.

174
00:12:52,772 --> 00:12:54,940
She seems more at ease somehow.

175
00:12:55,775 --> 00:12:59,278
- I guess Ga-eul isn't in pain anymore.
- Is that something a doctor should say?

176
00:12:59,361 --> 00:13:01,489
Dr. Park, you're gonna
land yourself in trouble.

177
00:13:33,687 --> 00:13:35,397
Get home safe, Dr. Gye.

178
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,874
12 HOURS BEFORE WORK STOPPAGE

179
00:13:55,668 --> 00:13:57,169
My puppy.

180
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:01,048
Ga-eul, can you hear
Grandma's voice, honey?

181
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:03,926
You mustn't fall asleep, okay, sweetie?

182
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:07,805
How unusual. Dr. Jo Won-jin
coming all this way to see this?

183
00:14:08,597 --> 00:14:11,183
Today's surgery requires me
to observe afterwards.

184
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:15,521
Gosh, even Dr. Jo Won-jin
hurried to be here,

185
00:14:15,604 --> 00:14:17,189
so where's the primary surgeon?

186
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:20,901
The bathhouse, that little jerk.

187
00:14:20,985 --> 00:14:24,530
<i>Not only that, she borrowed 1,500 won</i>
<i>from me to buy banana milk.</i>

188
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:27,950
<i>I didn't have change, so I gave her 2,000</i>
<i>and she left all giddy.</i>

189
00:14:28,033 --> 00:14:29,159
<i>Little mooch.</i>

190
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:32,246
Such a chump. The bathhouse, really?

191
00:14:32,329 --> 00:14:34,790
Borrowing 2000 won to get some milk?

192
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:37,751
Lucky her, getting out of here.

193
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:40,129
All us attending stayed back

194
00:14:40,212 --> 00:14:42,298
just in case something were to happen
during the strike.

195
00:14:43,382 --> 00:14:45,342
But we can't go on like this forever.

196
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:48,470
Well, the other side will probably
change their minds soon.

197
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:50,723
You really think
this strike'll last though?

198
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:52,892
It won't be long, last one was quick too.

199
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:54,435
But that was during the pandemic.

200
00:14:55,519 --> 00:14:57,563
Anybody's guess at this point, right?

201
00:14:57,646 --> 00:14:59,273
<i>The doors are now opening.</i>

202
00:15:00,858 --> 00:15:02,318
- Oh! What the…
- Hello.

203
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:05,863
I almost didn't recognize you
without your white coat on.

204
00:15:05,946 --> 00:15:07,698
I just took it off for a bit.
I'm still getting sort of--

205
00:15:07,781 --> 00:15:09,450
Not fully packed yet? Last minute move?

206
00:15:09,533 --> 00:15:10,618
Uh-huh.

207
00:15:10,701 --> 00:15:13,829
Of course. Whatever the task,
you see it through to the end, don't you?

208
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:16,206
That's our boy,
our irresistibly adorable Gyu.

209
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:19,460
Huh? You're good at your job
and super diligent.

210
00:15:30,804 --> 00:15:33,891
<i>- The doors are now open.</i>
- You can go ahead. Go wrap it up properly.

211
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:35,225
- Okay.
- You'll be back here to weigh in

212
00:15:35,309 --> 00:15:38,354
- on the emergency strategy vote anyways.
- Yeah, of course.

213
00:15:38,437 --> 00:15:39,396
Okay.

214
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:42,608
Hey!

215
00:15:43,525 --> 00:15:44,985
Answer your phone, Dr. Ma.

216
00:15:46,654 --> 00:15:48,280
Oh, sure thing.

217
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:50,741
Okay, get out of here.

218
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:55,120
TO THE WARD
VISITORS TO THE WARD FROM THE 2ND FLOOR

219
00:15:55,204 --> 00:15:59,166
I seriously can't spot that kid
at all without his white coat on.

220
00:15:59,249 --> 00:16:01,919
Ma Seong-gyu,
who got into med school on his third try.

221
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:04,546
The youngest boy of a single mother
who opened her own drug store.

222
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:08,217
God, that day…

223
00:16:09,176 --> 00:16:12,012
when we first called him
the irresistible Ma Seong-gyu.

224
00:16:12,096 --> 00:16:13,097
2 YEARS AGO

225
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:15,224
Uh, my mother, uh…

226
00:16:15,307 --> 00:16:19,269
…she wants me to work as a hospital doctor
instead of opening a clinic.

227
00:16:19,353 --> 00:16:20,562
- Oh.
- Right.

228
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:23,649
'Cause the doctor above her pharmacy,
she just has a really hard time.

229
00:16:23,732 --> 00:16:24,733
Oh.

230
00:16:24,817 --> 00:16:27,736
B-But me, I… I wanna become a doctor.

231
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:30,114
Seriously, like, a doctor doctor.

232
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:31,281
- Wow.
- Right.

233
00:16:31,865 --> 00:16:32,950
Seung-gwon!

234
00:16:33,033 --> 00:16:35,285
- D-Do you wanna see a picture of my niece?
- Hey, Seong-gyu.

235
00:16:35,369 --> 00:16:37,913
She's super cute. Here. Cute.

236
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:40,040
Isn't she so cute? She's really cute.

237
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:41,250
Cute.

238
00:16:41,333 --> 00:16:45,754
I'm cute too, right?
Cute, right? Aren't I super cute?

239
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:47,297
You're super cute, buddy.

240
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:48,882
Oh, you're so cute too, Seung-gwon.

241
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:50,843
- Eat up!
- Uh, yeah, he's cute. Yeah.

242
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:52,720
- Seung-gwon is so cute.
- Stop, let's stop it.

243
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:54,722
It'll be over and done soon.

244
00:16:54,805 --> 00:16:57,016
And still, for training
these kids don't have much time.

245
00:16:57,099 --> 00:17:01,270
If things keep getting pushed and delayed
they won't be able to handle it.

246
00:17:01,353 --> 00:17:03,397
It should be over within a week,
don't you think?

247
00:17:04,064 --> 00:17:06,025
<i>The doors are now opening.</i>

248
00:17:17,369 --> 00:17:20,205
- Oh, this is…
- This is just crazy.

249
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:33,427
- Wow!
- Whoa!

250
00:17:34,011 --> 00:17:37,556
Man, who would've thought
Eung-gu would treat us to pizza, huh?

251
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:39,433
How great is this?

252
00:17:39,516 --> 00:17:41,435
Congratulations on your new job,
Mr. Eung-gu.

253
00:17:42,019 --> 00:17:44,021
Why, I've never bought pizza
like this either.

254
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:46,523
I heard this places is great.
Grab some, Su-jeong.

255
00:17:46,607 --> 00:17:49,526
Oh, try the one with corn
and shrimp on top, Su-jeong.

256
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:51,779
It's the sweet and spicy one,
I bet you'd really like it.

257
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:55,157
And now…

258
00:17:55,866 --> 00:17:58,368
- Congrats, congrats.
- Oh, man, you guys.

259
00:18:02,164 --> 00:18:06,293
Ah! Today, Guseo University Medical Center
was saved by our Su-jeong.

260
00:18:06,376 --> 00:18:07,795
Ms. Jang, look at you go.

261
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:09,546
You'll get a big payday, huh?

262
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:11,590
Then give me 2,000 won to borrow.

263
00:18:14,802 --> 00:18:17,596
Ms. Jang, you're awfully quiet today.
What, you're not hungry?

264
00:18:18,847 --> 00:18:22,142
Earlier today, Director Bu Seung-gwon
brought up Dr. X.

265
00:18:22,226 --> 00:18:23,644
How much does he know?

266
00:18:23,727 --> 00:18:26,522
He's only seen the article.
He was just poking around.

267
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:29,483
I still feel uneasy,
though I gave it to him the best I could.

268
00:18:29,566 --> 00:18:32,236
To hear someone say that name now
and that it's come up at all…

269
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:34,863
It's like it's been eons.

270
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:36,907
I'm not exactly happy to hear it.

271
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:39,326
We should just
wash our hands of this hospital.

272
00:18:39,409 --> 00:18:40,702
We've already done our time.

273
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:42,871
We're not doing that.

274
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:55,551
I have to do this surgery.

275
00:18:56,593 --> 00:18:58,679
"'Lee Hyeon-a, eight years old."

276
00:18:58,762 --> 00:19:00,639
LEE HYEON-A F/08

277
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:15,195
MMT?

278
00:19:15,279 --> 00:19:18,824
An IMT is a tumor that can be
found in children, but this is…

279
00:19:18,907 --> 00:19:21,076
Gosh, for the tumor
to transform like this…

280
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:24,246
I knew they existed,
but never seen one myself.

281
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:28,876
This is a phenomenally
novel case, Su-jeong.

282
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:30,502
Fifteen centimeters.

283
00:19:30,586 --> 00:19:32,796
It's clamping the abdominal aorta.
Unreachable.

284
00:19:36,049 --> 00:19:38,260
Why are you sighing?
What's this mean in Western medicine?

285
00:19:38,343 --> 00:19:39,845
You can't leave me outta this.

286
00:19:42,055 --> 00:19:44,474
There is no surgical procedure for this,
Su-jeong.

287
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:45,976
There's just no way to do it.

288
00:19:46,059 --> 00:19:47,728
- I'll find one.
- No, you can't.

289
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:50,355
Why?

290
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:53,275
You'll look more like Dr. X to all them
than you do already.

291
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:07,915
Wait, you got a letter.

292
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,879
Just read it,
even if you don't write back.

293
00:20:22,763 --> 00:20:24,348
She can't even read this letter.

294
00:20:26,725 --> 00:20:28,727
Doing this won't bring him back to her.

295
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,826
No, no…

296
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:46,370
There must be some way.

297
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:49,748
Su-jeong, just get it together.

298
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:53,377
Work while ya eat?

299
00:20:55,045 --> 00:20:56,171
Here.

300
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:10,894
Thanks for bringing me this, Eung-gu.

301
00:21:10,978 --> 00:21:12,604
You get her perspective, don't you?

302
00:21:15,732 --> 00:21:19,111
All of us in this damn place are haunted
by our memories and pasts, aren't we?

303
00:21:22,864 --> 00:21:25,409
There's just no paradise
to escape to, is there, now?

304
00:21:26,034 --> 00:21:29,329
Yet, here I am,
I do feel happy now and again…

305
00:21:30,539 --> 00:21:32,499
Though I really shouldn't, I think.

306
00:21:34,167 --> 00:21:36,211
Auntie, me, and Mi-gyeong, too…

307
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:40,757
Su-jeong, we're all just afraid
we'll lose you again.

308
00:21:41,925 --> 00:21:45,929
They also say that you fear
more things as you get older.

309
00:21:50,142 --> 00:21:54,187
Now, either way,
this child's life is way more precious.

310
00:21:55,689 --> 00:21:58,942
Oh, dear. She's the age
my daughter was, back then.

311
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:05,574
Had she grown up,
she'd have reached adulthood already.

312
00:22:08,452 --> 00:22:11,747
I'd like to see this child grow up happy
and live a good life.

313
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:16,835
Find a way, however you need to.

314
00:22:16,918 --> 00:22:20,297
Gye Su-jeong, I know that you'll succeed.

315
00:22:35,812 --> 00:22:37,939
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

316
00:22:40,567 --> 00:22:41,568
Dr. Gye.

317
00:22:42,319 --> 00:22:45,197
What the… Where'd she go?

318
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:46,990
Why isn't she here? Where…

319
00:22:47,949 --> 00:22:50,035
Don't tell me she went
on strike with them, too?

320
00:22:54,414 --> 00:22:55,832
I knew it. I knew it.

321
00:22:59,795 --> 00:23:00,796
What the heck?

322
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:06,760
Dr. Park Tae-gyeong. Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

323
00:23:07,719 --> 00:23:09,846
Are you pretending you're asleep,
or can I just not wake you?

324
00:23:10,472 --> 00:23:12,057
Get up, please, Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

325
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:13,558
Oh…

326
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:15,352
Oh, Doctor Kim.

327
00:23:15,435 --> 00:23:16,937
Gosh, sorry, Doctor Kim.

328
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:20,232
It's just, uh, I couldn't find
a place to take a nap briefly,

329
00:23:20,315 --> 00:23:22,401
so I dozed off here for a sec…

330
00:23:22,484 --> 00:23:24,444
Hey, come on,
you couldn't find a place to nap?

331
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:27,447
What d'you mean? You've got
the staff and the on-call areas.

332
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:30,117
Oh, uh… it's just,
nobody else was in either--

333
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,952
So what if there were no people?
Who cares?

334
00:23:32,035 --> 00:23:34,037
He was scared because no one was there.

335
00:23:34,121 --> 00:23:35,455
But even if we're not taking patients,

336
00:23:35,539 --> 00:23:37,541
you'll always run into
some doctors and nurses in here.

337
00:23:37,624 --> 00:23:39,876
You think this is a dormitory?
Intern housing?

338
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:41,378
Hey, punk!

339
00:23:41,461 --> 00:23:43,630
Even if we're closed, we gotta stay ready
to take new patients in--

340
00:23:43,713 --> 00:23:44,881
Can we open the ER today?

341
00:23:44,965 --> 00:23:46,883
Director Bu, and the other
top-ranking doctors

342
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:48,677
are all staying behind
till the strike is through.

343
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:51,847
Regardless of them being here,
we still can't do anything,

344
00:23:51,930 --> 00:23:54,224
or take new patients,
'cause we can't give 'em follow-up care.

345
00:23:54,307 --> 00:23:57,102
Here I am, discouraging everyone.
Guess I shouldn't'a said a thing.

346
00:23:59,271 --> 00:24:01,022
Then to apologize, get me a coffee.

347
00:24:01,106 --> 00:24:03,233
And a sandwich, and an ice cream, too.

348
00:24:03,316 --> 00:24:06,027
- And some for him, too.
- Oh, no, I'm all right.

349
00:24:06,111 --> 00:24:07,904
I was wasting time hanging down here,

350
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:09,990
when really I should've
pulled it together sooner.

351
00:24:10,073 --> 00:24:12,159
- I'm gonna get some air real quick.
- Eh…

352
00:24:12,242 --> 00:24:13,952
You step outside
and they'll grab you, kid.

353
00:24:14,035 --> 00:24:15,036
Huh?

354
00:24:15,996 --> 00:24:17,706
Look, I've been pondering this
for a while.

355
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:22,252
We should've been selling some <i>gimbap</i>
or something out at the front door. Huh?

356
00:24:22,335 --> 00:24:24,254
Not to ER guests, to the journalists.

357
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:28,300
Man, we could've had so many team dinners
with that money. Seriously.

358
00:24:28,383 --> 00:24:30,510
That's the start of the strike.

359
00:24:31,303 --> 00:24:33,972
WORK STOPPAGE BEGINS

360
00:24:41,021 --> 00:24:42,314
TO OUR PATIENTS AND THEIR FAMILIES…

361
00:24:44,649 --> 00:24:46,193
RESIDENTS' STRIKE RESOLUTION
PREPARATORY COMMITTEE

362
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:47,944
What the hell?

363
00:24:58,497 --> 00:25:00,916
<i>Dr. Ma, I had a nosebleed</i>
<i>and got some some blood on here,</i>

364
00:25:00,999 --> 00:25:03,668
<i>so I wiped it off,</i>
<i>but the stain won't come out.</i>

365
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:06,838
<i>I covered it with this 'cause I was scared</i>
<i>I'd rip the page if I kept wiping it.</i>

366
00:25:06,922 --> 00:25:10,550
<i>Sorry. I saw there was a bloodstain</i>
<i>from a nosebleed on the back though, too.</i>

367
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:13,512
<i>Discovering that somehow comforted me.</i>

368
00:25:13,595 --> 00:25:17,224
<i>I thought, '"Even the irresistible Dr. Ma</i>
<i>is just a human being, like me.'"</i>

369
00:25:17,307 --> 00:25:20,769
<i>Thank you for lending me this book.</i>
<i>And thank you for the nosebleed, too.</i>

370
00:25:21,978 --> 00:25:25,357
<i>Dr. Ma, you'll continue to become</i>
<i>a great doctor.</i>

371
00:25:32,531 --> 00:25:34,866
This is somebody else's book.
Why's he damaging it?

372
00:25:46,753 --> 00:25:47,921
Ah, geez.

373
00:25:49,214 --> 00:25:50,298
Hey, you know how it is.

374
00:25:50,382 --> 00:25:52,676
All my surgeries got delayed
'cause of COVID and the strike,

375
00:25:52,759 --> 00:25:54,302
so I don't have time.

376
00:25:54,386 --> 00:25:57,889
Then tell 'em to sue me.
I did that surgery perfectly.

377
00:25:59,474 --> 00:26:00,725
Yeah, uh-huh, bye.

378
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:14,739
Oh, uh, hey, I-I need a new mask.
Bring it out here, ASAP.

379
00:26:14,823 --> 00:26:16,658
Take it to the bathroom
next to the staff room.

380
00:26:16,741 --> 00:26:19,119
I have an emergency surgery. Mm-hmm.

381
00:26:19,202 --> 00:26:20,203
For God's sake…

382
00:26:23,123 --> 00:26:25,875
Hey, did you do a PCR test? Negative?

383
00:26:25,959 --> 00:26:27,419
- Yeah, it was.
- Good.

384
00:26:27,502 --> 00:26:31,089
- Oh, and here's a new mask.
- Why?

385
00:26:31,172 --> 00:26:34,676
You need a mask to walk down
the hallway here. Aren't you in a hurry?

386
00:26:34,759 --> 00:26:36,886
- You're right.
- Here, have it.

387
00:26:36,970 --> 00:26:38,096
What about you?

388
00:26:38,179 --> 00:26:40,807
Oh, if that person comes up,
I'll use the one they bring.

389
00:26:40,890 --> 00:26:42,809
Oh! That's…

390
00:26:43,643 --> 00:26:45,645
- Thank you.
- Yeah, for sure.

391
00:26:46,271 --> 00:26:47,272
Thank you.

392
00:26:48,607 --> 00:26:50,942
- What's your name?
- Ah, it's Ma Seong-gyu. Nice to meet you.

393
00:26:51,026 --> 00:26:52,235
Ah, yeah, okay.

394
00:26:53,028 --> 00:26:55,113
Na Seon-gyun. Great. Thanks again.

395
00:26:57,782 --> 00:27:00,243
GENERAL SURGERY MA SEONG-GYU

396
00:27:23,683 --> 00:27:26,061
Dr. Ma, the Ministry of Health and Welfare

397
00:27:26,144 --> 00:27:28,313
just texted us
to come back to work immediately.

398
00:27:28,396 --> 00:27:30,565
Um, a text message to return to work?
W-What…

399
00:27:30,649 --> 00:27:32,150
YOU ARE CONFIRMED TO BE ABSENT
WITHOUT AUTHORIZATION

400
00:27:33,401 --> 00:27:35,195
YOU ARE ORDERED TO RESUME WORK
AND RETURN TO YOUR MEDICAL INSTITUTION

401
00:27:35,278 --> 00:27:36,279
"Medical license"?

402
00:27:36,363 --> 00:27:38,448
- I'll be going then.
- Uh-huh…

403
00:27:52,379 --> 00:27:54,381
WEDNESDAY, APRIL 29

404
00:27:57,967 --> 00:27:59,552
Ugh… Gosh.

405
00:28:01,805 --> 00:28:03,556
- Oh, he's coming out.
- Isn't that him?

406
00:28:05,100 --> 00:28:06,518
- Oh!
- He came out!

407
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:10,772
Does this mark the start of
the hospital walk-out?

408
00:28:10,855 --> 00:28:12,190
Tell us, are you really
walking off the job?

409
00:28:12,273 --> 00:28:13,274
Yes, that's what's happening.

410
00:28:13,358 --> 00:28:15,819
How extensive is
the work stoppage at this time?

411
00:28:15,902 --> 00:28:18,071
In this branch hospital,
about 85% have resigned.

412
00:28:18,154 --> 00:28:21,032
As head of the Korean Intern
Resident Association, any comments?

413
00:28:21,116 --> 00:28:23,910
Uh. Well, it's a truly regrettable day.

414
00:28:23,993 --> 00:28:25,620
To be walking out like this
is incredibly bleak.

415
00:28:25,704 --> 00:28:27,706
I'm sure we all feel
the same way about this.

416
00:28:27,789 --> 00:28:29,499
The government issued a blast message,

417
00:28:29,582 --> 00:28:31,501
<i>to warn all of us of their intent</i>
<i>to take legal action.</i>

418
00:28:31,584 --> 00:28:34,379
<i>And in light of that, we're committed</i>
<i>to continue our fight…</i>

419
00:28:34,462 --> 00:28:37,590
- Ugh, God, they're actually resigning.
<i>- We're going to put this to a vote…</i>

420
00:28:37,674 --> 00:28:39,050
MEDICAL STRIKE ESCALATES
WORK STOPPAGE BEGINS TODAY

421
00:28:39,134 --> 00:28:41,344
<i>- We'll hold a solidarity rally…</i>
- This will drag on.

422
00:28:41,428 --> 00:28:44,055
<i>…vote on the matter. And that includes</i>
<i>not only the senior doctors…</i>

423
00:28:44,139 --> 00:28:46,057
Well, shouldn't we take
this to Magnolia, Director?

424
00:28:46,141 --> 00:28:49,853
Magnolia is already supporting the strike,
so there's no point in trying that.

425
00:28:49,936 --> 00:28:51,187
They won't help us at all.

426
00:28:52,439 --> 00:28:54,065
But if we can't reel in this mess,

427
00:28:55,567 --> 00:28:58,319
be sure that closing us down
will re-enter the conversation.

428
00:28:58,403 --> 00:29:00,363
Yes?

429
00:29:00,447 --> 00:29:03,616
<i>This strike is our last resort to prevent</i>
<i>the collapse of the healthcare system.</i>

430
00:29:09,205 --> 00:29:11,958
It's quite early, isn't it?
What brings you here, Dr. Gye?

431
00:29:14,544 --> 00:29:17,255
I'm allowed to perform
any surgery that I want to.

432
00:29:18,256 --> 00:29:19,549
That's a clause in our agreement.

433
00:29:24,304 --> 00:29:25,722
LEE HYEON-A F/08

434
00:29:25,805 --> 00:29:27,182
MALIGNANT NEOPLASM OF THE CONNECTIVE
AND SOFT TISSUE OF THE ABDOMEN

435
00:29:27,265 --> 00:29:28,850
Oh, this. Well, this surgery
is just not going to--

436
00:29:28,933 --> 00:29:32,645
You also said, if within six hours
Miss Ya Ga-eul's surgery was completed,

437
00:29:32,729 --> 00:29:36,191
that you'd be more flexible
relating to the terms of my contract.

438
00:29:36,900 --> 00:29:38,568
It took five hours and 20 minutes.

439
00:29:38,651 --> 00:29:41,488
Well, then, you choose this operation?

440
00:29:41,571 --> 00:29:43,031
I do.

441
00:29:43,865 --> 00:29:47,285
No way. This patient's been
cleared for discharge already. Come on.

442
00:29:47,368 --> 00:29:49,120
You know of this case, Dr. Do?

443
00:29:49,204 --> 00:29:51,456
I… I was requested to consult on it,

444
00:29:51,998 --> 00:29:54,626
except, I refused the case,
because it was clearly hopeless.

445
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:57,462
I'm sure they gave it to us
when the main hospital said the same.

446
00:29:57,545 --> 00:30:02,008
But Dr. Gye Su-jeong here has apparently
determined that there's hope.

447
00:30:02,091 --> 00:30:03,092
I'll do this operation.

448
00:30:03,176 --> 00:30:05,929
- No! No way. This is--
- It's your assignment, then.

449
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:12,352
A conference is in order.

450
00:30:18,399 --> 00:30:20,777
Persuade the other doctors
this surgery can be done.

451
00:30:21,569 --> 00:30:23,071
CASE 1 LEE HYEON-A F/08

452
00:30:23,154 --> 00:30:26,407
This conference was put together
on short notice by special request.

453
00:30:26,491 --> 00:30:29,202
I gathered everyone
who's still here at the hospital,

454
00:30:29,285 --> 00:30:32,413
and could help us with this surgery.
So, please, I'd like your full attention.

455
00:30:32,497 --> 00:30:35,416
Director, but, uh,
in regards to this surgery,

456
00:30:35,500 --> 00:30:38,336
who would lead the team?
Who is the main surgeon operating?

457
00:30:39,003 --> 00:30:41,089
Dr. Gye Su-jeong is the primary surgeon.

458
00:30:44,092 --> 00:30:45,802
The patient is eight years old.

459
00:30:45,885 --> 00:30:47,887
Her name's Lee Hyeon-a.
She has cancerous myofibroblastoma.

460
00:30:47,971 --> 00:30:50,056
A RARE MALIGNANT SOFT TISSUE TUMOR THAT
SHOWS CHARACTERISTICS OF MYOFIBROBLASTS

461
00:30:50,139 --> 00:30:53,685
The spread extends to the IVC,
caudate lobe, portal vein,

462
00:30:53,768 --> 00:30:58,273
SMV, SMA, the pancreatic head,
and mesocolon as well.

463
00:30:58,356 --> 00:30:59,899
This was a prior case we turned down.

464
00:30:59,983 --> 00:31:02,527
It'd spread all around,
and it's in an inoperable location.

465
00:31:02,610 --> 00:31:06,823
Well, it absolutely is.
It's about the worst it could be.

466
00:31:10,034 --> 00:31:14,330
By my estimation,
three months is the most time she has.

467
00:31:15,373 --> 00:31:19,085
Dr. Gye, everyone here is sorry
about this poor child's prognosis,

468
00:31:19,168 --> 00:31:21,421
- but that doesn't mean--
- The tumor is already 15 centimeters.

469
00:31:21,504 --> 00:31:25,049
Vital arteries are connected through that
region, so we'd need to block circulation.

470
00:31:25,133 --> 00:31:27,886
This operation can't be done.
It's impossible, period.

471
00:31:27,969 --> 00:31:29,762
- There's no method for it--
- There is a method.

472
00:31:29,846 --> 00:31:31,514
You're just unaware of it.

473
00:31:36,603 --> 00:31:39,147
Ex vivo multivisceral resection,
followed by an orthotropic autotransplant.

474
00:31:39,230 --> 00:31:40,690
EX VIVO MULTIVISCERAL RESECTION
AND AUTOTRANSPLANTATION

475
00:31:40,773 --> 00:31:42,400
That is the surgical method.

476
00:31:42,483 --> 00:31:45,236
Ex vivo multi… resected… What method?

477
00:31:47,196 --> 00:31:51,701
First, we'd begin the resection
and remove the stomach, pancreas, spleen,

478
00:31:51,784 --> 00:31:54,454
liver, colon, and finally, the tumors.

479
00:31:55,204 --> 00:31:57,498
For this surgery,
six removals will be needed.

480
00:31:58,917 --> 00:31:59,918
Wait, what?

481
00:32:03,838 --> 00:32:06,883
Wait, is that even possible?
Does that surgery exist?

482
00:32:06,966 --> 00:32:10,595
It doesn't. That's completely new.
I've never heard about it.

483
00:32:10,678 --> 00:32:13,973
Otherwise, if we try to access the tumor
while inside the body,

484
00:32:14,057 --> 00:32:16,768
we'll spend too much time
trying to remove the tumor,

485
00:32:16,851 --> 00:32:19,479
because it's entangled
with blood vessels and organs.

486
00:32:19,562 --> 00:32:22,523
Blood flow to the organs will be blocked,
allowing necrosis to begin.

487
00:32:22,607 --> 00:32:24,609
Everyone knows that. Come on, Dr. Gye!
That doesn't mean

488
00:32:24,692 --> 00:32:26,778
- you use this type of method--
- First,

489
00:32:26,861 --> 00:32:30,615
once we're inside, we will then extract
all of the organs from the abdomen,

490
00:32:30,698 --> 00:32:34,410
precisely remove the tumors out of each,
then, autotransplant.

491
00:32:34,494 --> 00:32:37,580
I think you're thinking of this like it's
just a regular organ transplant surgery--

492
00:32:37,664 --> 00:32:39,290
Well, that'd be right.

493
00:32:39,999 --> 00:32:43,044
Well, I mean, just how many blood vessels
are you planning to cut and reconnect?

494
00:32:43,127 --> 00:32:45,004
- Most likely a lot.
- You're crazy!

495
00:32:45,088 --> 00:32:47,340
- Dr. Gye, this is mental--
- How long will it take?

496
00:32:50,176 --> 00:32:51,678
Fifteen hours, I'd say.

497
00:32:51,761 --> 00:32:53,012
What 15 hours?

498
00:32:53,096 --> 00:32:56,432
It takes around six hours just
to get two organs transplanted.

499
00:32:56,516 --> 00:32:57,850
Talk sense, there's just no way.

500
00:32:57,934 --> 00:33:00,311
Please, Director.
It's unreasonable and dangerous.

501
00:33:00,395 --> 00:33:03,022
Yes, it's a very dangerous operation.

502
00:33:03,106 --> 00:33:04,732
Have you done it before?

503
00:33:04,816 --> 00:33:07,110
Surely you did,
that's why you're suggesting it, right?

504
00:33:07,193 --> 00:33:08,528
- No, I have not.
- What?

505
00:33:08,611 --> 00:33:11,030
You're suggesting a surgery
you've never done before?

506
00:33:11,114 --> 00:33:13,491
This… This whole procedure
will end up failing.

507
00:33:13,574 --> 00:33:15,326
Surely everybody here
thinks the same thing.

508
00:33:26,254 --> 00:33:28,589
What's wrong? Don't wanna say it? Huh?

509
00:33:28,673 --> 00:33:31,759
"Oh, don't worry, 'cause I never fail."
Those words.

510
00:33:33,011 --> 00:33:34,220
Come on, say 'em.

511
00:33:43,229 --> 00:33:44,397
I have to assemble a team.

512
00:33:52,697 --> 00:33:54,198
The six organs removed from the body

513
00:33:54,282 --> 00:33:56,993
will be kept in a preservation solution
at a low temperature,

514
00:33:57,076 --> 00:34:00,288
and the team operating
is going to work together, ex vivo,

515
00:34:00,371 --> 00:34:02,665
to remove the tumors
and reconstruct the vasculature.

516
00:34:05,168 --> 00:34:09,213
During that process,
the child can only hold out for so long…

517
00:34:09,297 --> 00:34:13,092
so, to cut time, the operating surgeons
will work together to get it done quicker.

518
00:34:13,176 --> 00:34:15,803
Tumor-involved vessels will be
replaced with synthetic vascular grafts,

519
00:34:15,887 --> 00:34:18,097
then the reconstructed organs
will be put back,

520
00:34:18,181 --> 00:34:21,392
and the blood vessels anastomosed
to restore circulation.

521
00:34:21,476 --> 00:34:25,104
And what if there's extreme caudal-side
infiltration on the pancreatic tumor?

522
00:34:25,188 --> 00:34:26,189
Then what?

523
00:34:26,272 --> 00:34:27,732
Then we'll have to take
the whole thing out.

524
00:34:27,815 --> 00:34:29,859
However, to prevent that, we'll perform

525
00:34:29,942 --> 00:34:32,779
- a biopsy during the surgery--
- The IRB will decide.

526
00:34:32,862 --> 00:34:34,113
A COMMITTEE THAT REVIEWS AND APPROVES
ETHICS AND SAFETY OF CLINICAL RESEARCH

527
00:34:36,741 --> 00:34:41,245
All new surgical methods must always
be IRB-cleared prior to operating.

528
00:34:41,329 --> 00:34:43,247
You can't call this
a completely new surgical method.

529
00:34:43,331 --> 00:34:47,168
When it's an unprecedented operation,
it needs to be cleared by the IRB.

530
00:34:47,835 --> 00:34:51,130
We'll gather the surgery materials and
we'll send it with the patient's consent.

531
00:34:51,214 --> 00:34:53,049
And how long will we need to wait?

532
00:34:53,132 --> 00:34:55,635
It usually takes around a week,
so wait a bit.

533
00:34:55,718 --> 00:34:57,678
That's too long. There's no time to waste.

534
00:34:58,513 --> 00:34:59,514
Dr. Gye Su-jeong,

535
00:35:01,474 --> 00:35:04,977
do you expect anyone to come
participate in this risky operation?

536
00:35:06,395 --> 00:35:08,064
Are you saying you'll do this surgery,

537
00:35:08,147 --> 00:35:10,108
where absolutely
nothing can be guaranteed,

538
00:35:10,191 --> 00:35:13,277
and put this eight-year-old
patient's life up as collateral

539
00:35:13,361 --> 00:35:16,030
derailing your own career,
and your colleagues' in the process?

540
00:35:19,784 --> 00:35:23,871
I'm betting on my skills, along with
my reputation, to do as I swore to.

541
00:35:24,872 --> 00:35:27,875
Director, I'm saying I want to save
the life of an eight-year-old patient.

542
00:35:28,835 --> 00:35:30,545
Then wait till it's cleared.

543
00:35:30,628 --> 00:35:35,049
Don't you need a team and an open OR
available with no limit on time?

544
00:35:36,134 --> 00:35:38,177
Go through the process,
and get it cleared with the IRB.

545
00:35:38,261 --> 00:35:41,305
Director, please.
The child doesn't have time for that.

546
00:35:42,306 --> 00:35:44,142
Will you be able to do it
the day after next?

547
00:35:45,685 --> 00:35:47,812
Oh, that's right,
that's the one day you can use

548
00:35:47,895 --> 00:35:50,690
the biggest OR for the whole day,
yeah, that's true.

549
00:35:50,773 --> 00:35:53,401
All the other ORs are empty that day, too.

550
00:35:54,735 --> 00:35:56,821
The hospital-wide
resignation vote is that day.

551
00:35:56,904 --> 00:35:58,531
There was just a blast message about it.

552
00:35:59,407 --> 00:36:01,784
The rest of you must have
gotten it, too, right?

553
00:36:01,868 --> 00:36:03,411
Except Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

554
00:36:04,453 --> 00:36:08,249
I assume you'll join the rally and strike,
with how much you support other doctors.

555
00:36:11,127 --> 00:36:13,379
Shall we ask now,
and see who'd be willing?

556
00:36:16,007 --> 00:36:17,091
Then, let's count.

557
00:36:17,842 --> 00:36:20,553
Are there any doctors
willing to join this surgery

558
00:36:21,929 --> 00:36:23,556
as the lead surgeon for this operation?

559
00:36:35,568 --> 00:36:37,612
Submit the materials and wait.

560
00:36:38,362 --> 00:36:39,947
Let's convince them later, one by one.

561
00:36:40,531 --> 00:36:42,283
It's not the right time here.

562
00:36:42,366 --> 00:36:44,660
Nobody'll raise their hand right now.

563
00:36:51,459 --> 00:36:54,212
There's nobody here who will help us.

564
00:36:55,504 --> 00:37:00,176
The IRB isn't the problem, or the strike,
it's these people, right here.

565
00:37:00,259 --> 00:37:02,220
I'll ask you all yet again.

566
00:37:02,303 --> 00:37:05,556
Do we have any doctors here
who'd be willing to join us

567
00:37:05,640 --> 00:37:07,683
as the principal surgeon
on this operation?

568
00:37:27,495 --> 00:37:30,122
CASE 1 LEE HYEON-A F/08

569
00:38:03,531 --> 00:38:04,907
I'm begging you.

570
00:38:38,399 --> 00:38:40,901
This is horribly unfair of you all.

571
00:38:40,985 --> 00:38:44,488
Even if this surgery may be hopeless,
how can you act like such cowards?

572
00:38:44,572 --> 00:38:46,282
If you lack the confidence to do it,

573
00:38:46,365 --> 00:38:48,200
shouldn't you at least be
cheering on the person

574
00:38:48,284 --> 00:38:50,119
with the courage to take responsibility?

575
00:38:50,202 --> 00:38:53,748
A rally? The IRB? Those are all excuses.

576
00:38:53,831 --> 00:38:58,210
I'll remember every last one of you guys
walking out that door right now.

577
00:38:58,794 --> 00:39:00,671
Shame on you all for running.

578
00:39:08,179 --> 00:39:11,599
After all of that,
how could no one step forward?

579
00:39:11,682 --> 00:39:13,934
After she practically begged on her knees.

580
00:39:14,018 --> 00:39:16,896
I wasn't on my knees.
I was just bowing a little bit.

581
00:39:24,570 --> 00:39:26,489
This is great, despite everything.

582
00:39:29,283 --> 00:39:31,660
You're incredible, Dr. Gye, truly.

583
00:39:31,744 --> 00:39:35,414
You were incredible earlier.
Like, I really don't have the words.

584
00:39:35,498 --> 00:39:38,000
Yeah. I agree with Tae-gyeong.

585
00:39:39,418 --> 00:39:42,546
Dr. Gye, what you did takes courage.

586
00:39:43,839 --> 00:39:45,257
You were incredible too, Dr. Jo.

587
00:39:45,925 --> 00:39:48,386
Everyone was just walking out
and you suddenly said,

588
00:39:48,469 --> 00:39:49,929
"Shame on you all for running."

589
00:39:52,181 --> 00:39:54,600
But, do you think
they really feel any shame?

590
00:39:54,683 --> 00:39:55,684
What do you think?

591
00:39:55,768 --> 00:39:59,814
So, we just wait for the IRB, then?
There's no way that we can wait that long.

592
00:40:01,232 --> 00:40:03,609
When a person acts out of character,
they die, you know.

593
00:40:03,692 --> 00:40:07,571
- Hey, wait you're not dead, right?
- Not dead, I'm thinking.

594
00:40:07,655 --> 00:40:08,823
Oh, what's on your mind?

595
00:40:09,407 --> 00:40:10,658
Solo surgery.

596
00:40:10,741 --> 00:40:12,785
PERFORMED BY SURGEON,
WITHOUT ANY SURGICAL ASSISTANTS

597
00:40:22,294 --> 00:40:24,755
If the IRB says yes,
nobody will come anyway.

598
00:40:25,256 --> 00:40:27,716
Not nobody, I definitely would.
You know that, right?

599
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:31,053
Though, I guess I probably
won't be much help, would I?

600
00:40:31,137 --> 00:40:32,179
Let's go.

601
00:40:33,013 --> 00:40:34,014
But, Dr. Jo…

602
00:40:37,184 --> 00:40:39,854
Let's do it.
I'll open the OR for you right now.

603
00:40:39,937 --> 00:40:42,231
All we're hearing is "it won't work"
at every turn.

604
00:40:42,314 --> 00:40:44,233
That doesn't mean
we should sit and do nothing.

605
00:40:45,067 --> 00:40:47,236
Let's get whatever materials
they need to look through,

606
00:40:47,319 --> 00:40:49,029
and get ready to operate solo.

607
00:40:49,113 --> 00:40:51,031
Let's go prep for this operation
the right way.

608
00:40:51,115 --> 00:40:53,534
All surgeries were canceled,
I've got an empty day,

609
00:40:53,617 --> 00:40:54,785
so I'm wide open.

610
00:40:58,038 --> 00:40:59,623
You said you don't fail, right?

611
00:41:00,541 --> 00:41:03,127
Today, you'll learn,
I do not back down in anything.

612
00:41:06,005 --> 00:41:07,548
All right, now get up!

613
00:41:07,631 --> 00:41:10,176
Hey! Let's go, come on!
There's no time to waste!

614
00:41:10,259 --> 00:41:11,385
Get up already, Dr. Gye!

615
00:41:20,352 --> 00:41:21,353
Let's go.

616
00:41:24,148 --> 00:41:25,274
Yup!

617
00:41:28,110 --> 00:41:30,779
<i>And after having looked</i>
<i>at the scans myself,</i>

618
00:41:30,863 --> 00:41:33,157
<i>I saw there was clearly an irregularity.</i>

619
00:41:34,408 --> 00:41:37,328
<i>In the human hand,</i>
<i>there are so many tendons, ligaments,</i>

620
00:41:37,411 --> 00:41:39,788
<i>and different types of</i>
<i>mechanical things happening,</i>

621
00:41:39,872 --> 00:41:41,832
<i>that it becomes incredibly complicated…</i>

622
00:41:41,916 --> 00:41:43,250
Su-jeong.

623
00:41:43,334 --> 00:41:44,460
<i>We had to act fast…</i>

624
00:41:44,543 --> 00:41:47,463
If you do that surgery,
you really will be fired.

625
00:41:47,546 --> 00:41:50,508
<i>In the patient's case,</i>
<i>this meant a thumb surgery.</i>

626
00:41:54,512 --> 00:41:56,347
<i>So, for the functionality of the hand,</i>

627
00:41:56,430 --> 00:41:58,641
<i>the thumb surgery is the most important.</i>

628
00:41:58,724 --> 00:42:00,935
<i>The paralysis hasn't completely gone away,</i>

629
00:42:01,018 --> 00:42:02,520
<i>and what's called</i>
<i>a contracture release surgery…</i>

630
00:42:02,603 --> 00:42:04,271
Hey! Aren't you gonna answer me?

631
00:42:04,355 --> 00:42:06,899
<i>…is the only thing that can fix it.</i>

632
00:42:10,236 --> 00:42:11,403
Clamp the IVC.

633
00:42:13,447 --> 00:42:14,782
Clamp the celiac trunk.

634
00:42:17,993 --> 00:42:20,746
Connect the HTK. Beginning the perfusion.

635
00:42:23,999 --> 00:42:25,668
Beginning the reconstruction.

636
00:42:28,170 --> 00:42:29,922
We start with liver mobilization.

637
00:42:30,464 --> 00:42:33,384
- Dissect the vessels first, then--
- Again.

638
00:42:34,385 --> 00:42:36,887
We need to cut down
by half an hour, at least.

639
00:42:36,971 --> 00:42:39,807
There just isn't enough time.

640
00:42:41,058 --> 00:42:43,561
No matter what I do,
I can't cut down the time.

641
00:42:45,020 --> 00:42:46,939
Even if you don't have
a fellow primary surgeon,

642
00:42:47,022 --> 00:42:49,191
I think you at least need
a skilled assistant.

643
00:42:52,194 --> 00:42:53,237
Let's try this again.

644
00:42:57,616 --> 00:43:00,327
Wow, it's huge in here!

645
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:03,497
Mommy, it's way bigger
than it looked from over there.

646
00:43:05,916 --> 00:43:07,459
Hello, Miss Doctor.

647
00:43:09,712 --> 00:43:11,922
Hyeon-a, we thought
you might feel less scared

648
00:43:12,006 --> 00:43:14,300
if you came in to see the room first.
Are you feeling okay?

649
00:43:14,383 --> 00:43:16,468
I'm not scared at all, Doctor.

650
00:43:16,552 --> 00:43:19,930
A little while ago I saw her
do surgery on my Snuggles.

651
00:43:20,514 --> 00:43:21,724
Ah.

652
00:43:22,808 --> 00:43:25,644
So, you'll just lay down there
and have a good sleep,

653
00:43:25,728 --> 00:43:28,147
and by the time you wake up,
it'll be over.

654
00:43:38,532 --> 00:43:39,950
Dr. Gye Su-Jeong?

655
00:43:40,826 --> 00:43:41,827
Yeah?

656
00:43:41,910 --> 00:43:46,415
Thank you for doing surgery
on Ga-eul, you saved her life.

657
00:43:47,499 --> 00:43:50,419
And thank you for doing surgery
on Snuggles, too.

658
00:43:50,502 --> 00:43:51,879
He's a lot better now.

659
00:43:52,588 --> 00:43:57,509
And also for agreeing
to do the surgery on me

660
00:43:57,593 --> 00:43:59,470
when none of the other doctors would.

661
00:44:01,096 --> 00:44:02,181
Thank you, Doctor.

662
00:44:05,559 --> 00:44:08,187
Oh, she kept saying
she wanted to thank you.

663
00:44:08,896 --> 00:44:10,731
You can thank her after the surgery.

664
00:44:11,982 --> 00:44:13,984
But I might not wake up from it.

665
00:44:32,211 --> 00:44:33,629
That won't happen, Hyeon-a.

666
00:44:35,255 --> 00:44:37,508
Know why? Because…

667
00:44:38,884 --> 00:44:40,511
I never, ever fail.

668
00:44:48,352 --> 00:44:50,396
I won't let any operation fail.

669
00:44:50,896 --> 00:44:52,773
I won't let any operation fail.

670
00:44:53,565 --> 00:44:55,442
I won't let any operation fail.

671
00:44:56,276 --> 00:44:59,071
I… won't…

672
00:44:59,780 --> 00:45:01,323
let any operation fail.

673
00:45:07,454 --> 00:45:09,665
She can't have snacks at night anymore.

674
00:45:09,748 --> 00:45:11,917
Once they get approval,
they'll do the surgery.

675
00:45:12,668 --> 00:45:15,379
We don't know when they will,
so she has to fast--

676
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:18,549
Hey, don't cry.

677
00:45:18,632 --> 00:45:21,135
Even Hyeon-a isn't crying,
so her dad shouldn't be either.

678
00:45:21,677 --> 00:45:22,803
We shouldn't cry.

679
00:45:23,637 --> 00:45:25,806
How's the injury you got
at the construction site?

680
00:45:25,889 --> 00:45:26,890
Doing better yet?

681
00:45:28,350 --> 00:45:31,979
Please go to the ER. We've still got
a little bit of money left.

682
00:45:32,062 --> 00:45:34,064
Don't take on any more work, okay?

683
00:45:35,816 --> 00:45:37,860
Let's video call tomorrow at lunch.

684
00:45:37,943 --> 00:45:39,653
I know you miss her a bunch, huh?

685
00:45:46,118 --> 00:45:48,078
Hey, come on, she isn't dead.

686
00:45:48,620 --> 00:45:49,788
Really, don't cry.

687
00:45:50,998 --> 00:45:52,374
I said don't cry.

688
00:45:53,292 --> 00:45:55,377
Hey! Don't cry. Seriously!

689
00:46:04,386 --> 00:46:06,096
So, what'd they say? Anything?

690
00:46:07,014 --> 00:46:08,724
They said, 'cause of the strike,

691
00:46:08,807 --> 00:46:10,601
getting the IRB to convene right now
would be extremely hard.

692
00:46:10,684 --> 00:46:11,894
What about the strike?

693
00:46:11,977 --> 00:46:15,063
They said according to how tomorrow goes,
hospital staffing might be reconsidered--

694
00:46:15,147 --> 00:46:16,398
Right, I'll go jump on that.

695
00:46:16,482 --> 00:46:18,567
- Oh, Dr. Jo--
- I can't with these people. I swear.

696
00:46:31,455 --> 00:46:32,456
Here you go.

697
00:46:32,539 --> 00:46:35,834
Dr. Gye, when you're eating,
you should just focus on your food,

698
00:46:35,918 --> 00:46:37,669
or else you'll get indigestion.

699
00:46:37,753 --> 00:46:40,297
Plus, if you eat while lost in thought
you'll bite your tongue.

700
00:46:42,424 --> 00:46:44,426
RESEARCH ADMINISTRATION BUILDING

701
00:46:47,763 --> 00:46:49,723
Oh, you're just now heading out?

702
00:46:49,807 --> 00:46:51,767
Well, everyone else's working so hard.

703
00:46:53,143 --> 00:46:54,561
Are you also heading out for the night?

704
00:46:54,645 --> 00:46:56,355
I'm heading back home quick.

705
00:46:56,438 --> 00:46:58,398
There are just some essentials
I need to bring in.

706
00:46:59,983 --> 00:47:00,984
Dr. Do…

707
00:47:03,237 --> 00:47:04,738
you should treat me to a drink.

708
00:47:05,948 --> 00:47:06,990
You sure?

709
00:47:11,912 --> 00:47:14,331
BUDAE JJIGAE

710
00:47:33,767 --> 00:47:36,520
I'm not buying you a drink
from here because I'm broke.

711
00:47:36,603 --> 00:47:38,605
This is the only place
with non-alcoholic beer.

712
00:47:38,689 --> 00:47:42,067
Regular beer would work just fine.
Or, soju is good, too.

713
00:47:42,150 --> 00:47:44,945
Don't say that, please, sir,
we seriously can't do that now.

714
00:47:45,028 --> 00:47:46,697
Your wife would choke me out if I let you.

715
00:47:48,699 --> 00:47:50,576
Here, here, drink. Oh!

716
00:47:52,202 --> 00:47:55,414
Can I get you a snack with that, sir?

717
00:47:56,290 --> 00:47:58,709
Well, you're actually
quite into your snacks, aren't you?

718
00:48:00,085 --> 00:48:03,547
Even at my age, Director, I do quite enjoy
a snack every now and then.

719
00:48:17,853 --> 00:48:22,024
So, that huge rally, the one being held
in the conference hall.

720
00:48:22,107 --> 00:48:24,067
I heard that Magnolia will be attending.

721
00:48:25,027 --> 00:48:27,613
That'd be the perfect time for persuasion,

722
00:48:27,696 --> 00:48:29,072
to discuss the hospital closure.

723
00:48:39,833 --> 00:48:41,585
I expected I would feel good.

724
00:48:44,338 --> 00:48:47,215
I thought that in seeing
Gye Su-jeong be humiliated

725
00:48:48,717 --> 00:48:50,969
I'd feel good on the inside.

726
00:48:56,391 --> 00:48:58,226
That is sincerely what I thought.

727
00:49:06,944 --> 00:49:09,696
These really taste bad to me now.

728
00:49:11,239 --> 00:49:13,033
Even though I really like snacks.

729
00:49:18,163 --> 00:49:21,208
<i>If that happens,</i>
<i>what was once perfectly fine</i>

730
00:49:21,291 --> 00:49:24,044
<i>begins to disappear as the brain shrinks.</i>

731
00:49:24,127 --> 00:49:25,837
<i>The shrinking of the brain,</i>
<i>in proper terms,</i>

732
00:49:25,921 --> 00:49:28,048
<i>means that the brain is atrophying.</i>

733
00:49:28,131 --> 00:49:29,549
<i>This is one of the typical early changes</i>

734
00:49:29,633 --> 00:49:31,343
<i>- in dementia.</i>
<i>- </i>Su-jeong.

735
00:49:31,426 --> 00:49:34,763
<i>An MRI can show the process</i>
<i>of the brain atrophying.</i>

736
00:49:34,846 --> 00:49:36,974
<i>This process can damage</i>
<i>the nerve cells that exist in the--</i>

737
00:49:37,057 --> 00:49:40,852
If you do this reckless operation that
isn't cleared with the IRB, and you fail,

738
00:49:40,936 --> 00:49:42,729
you'll be the one they blame
for everything.

739
00:49:42,813 --> 00:49:44,731
Well, actually…

740
00:49:44,815 --> 00:49:47,150
Dr. Jo and the young doctor
will go down with you.

741
00:49:47,234 --> 00:49:49,111
<i>This leads to Alzheimer's disease.</i>

742
00:49:49,194 --> 00:49:52,447
<i>However, what we're looking at here</i>
<i>isn't a neurodegenerative disease…</i>

743
00:49:52,531 --> 00:49:56,284
If someone sues you for it later,
what about our locum tenens agency?

744
00:49:56,368 --> 00:49:57,619
<i>…reactive oxygen species.</i>

745
00:49:57,703 --> 00:50:00,789
<i>Now, let's have a look at</i>
<i>how harmful these reactive oxygen…</i>

746
00:50:00,872 --> 00:50:03,667
Don't worry, Su-jeong.
We're gonna be okay.

747
00:50:03,750 --> 00:50:05,335
Keep outta this, both of you.

748
00:50:06,628 --> 00:50:08,046
<i>Let's take a look at what changes occur</i>

749
00:50:08,130 --> 00:50:11,717
<i>when we expose fish embryos</i>
<i>to reactive oxygen species.</i>

750
00:50:11,800 --> 00:50:14,094
I'm terminating your contract
with the hospital tomorrow,

751
00:50:14,177 --> 00:50:15,262
so that's that.

752
00:50:15,762 --> 00:50:17,347
Wait a minute, Auntie.

753
00:50:17,431 --> 00:50:20,308
<i>…because it consumes</i>
<i>around 20% of the body's oxygen,</i>

754
00:50:20,392 --> 00:50:22,853
<i>but has low antioxidant defenses.</i>

755
00:50:22,936 --> 00:50:25,355
<i>This leaves the brain vulnerable</i>
<i>to oxidative stress,</i>

756
00:50:25,439 --> 00:50:27,691
<i>resulting in the destruction</i>
<i>of cell membranes…</i>

757
00:50:27,774 --> 00:50:28,900
That's her first doll.

758
00:50:28,984 --> 00:50:30,819
<i>…degrading of structural proteins,</i>
<i>and breaking down…</i>

759
00:50:30,902 --> 00:50:32,571
It could be her last one.

760
00:50:32,654 --> 00:50:34,114
<i>Here, we have a tuna embryo</i>

761
00:50:34,197 --> 00:50:37,451
<i>who's ROS exposure has been limited</i>
<i>to only what's naturally produced.</i>

762
00:50:38,618 --> 00:50:42,789
<i>The second embryo has been regularly</i>
<i>exposed to reactive oxygen species,</i>

763
00:50:42,873 --> 00:50:46,585
<i>and as a result, we can see that atrophy</i>
<i>has taken place in the brain,</i>

764
00:50:46,668 --> 00:50:48,628
<i>shrinking the overall volume…</i>

765
00:50:49,880 --> 00:50:51,089
- Hey, Mom.
- Hm?

766
00:50:51,173 --> 00:50:52,966
I'm so hungry I can't sleep.

767
00:50:53,633 --> 00:50:55,427
I'm also too hungry to go to bed, hon.

768
00:50:55,510 --> 00:50:58,180
No, Mom, but you can eat, can't you?

769
00:50:58,263 --> 00:50:59,306
What? No.

770
00:51:01,933 --> 00:51:04,519
Here's an idea,
should we get something to eat?

771
00:51:04,603 --> 00:51:06,563
We don't know
if your surgery's tomorrow or not.

772
00:51:06,646 --> 00:51:07,939
I don't wanna.

773
00:51:08,023 --> 00:51:10,734
Doctor lady's working super hard,
isn't she?

774
00:51:10,817 --> 00:51:12,360
I can handle the hunger.

775
00:51:14,071 --> 00:51:16,948
Oh… Gummies.

776
00:51:18,575 --> 00:51:19,868
I gotta be good.

777
00:51:21,661 --> 00:51:23,789
Okay. We'll do it as a team, then.

778
00:51:25,916 --> 00:51:27,042
- Hey, Mama.
- Hm?

779
00:51:27,125 --> 00:51:28,627
- Do you think, that…
- Yeah?

780
00:51:28,710 --> 00:51:31,171
…you'd wanna play a game
where we say what we wanna eat?

781
00:51:31,254 --> 00:51:32,798
Oh, would I?

782
00:51:32,881 --> 00:51:34,466
Hmm…

783
00:51:34,966 --> 00:51:36,343
Uh…

784
00:51:36,968 --> 00:51:38,512
Uh…

785
00:51:39,096 --> 00:51:40,388
<i>Tang-Sue-yuk!</i>

786
00:51:40,472 --> 00:51:42,808
I could go for some of that too!

787
00:51:42,891 --> 00:51:44,851
I chose that! You gotta say your own!

788
00:51:44,935 --> 00:51:46,103
Hmm…

789
00:51:46,770 --> 00:51:48,688
- Oh no, I think I lose!
- Yay!

790
00:51:48,772 --> 00:51:51,358
I knew I was good at that!

791
00:51:51,441 --> 00:51:53,860
Wow, Hyeon-a, you won again!

792
00:52:06,039 --> 00:52:07,082
Hyeon-a.

793
00:52:07,958 --> 00:52:09,209
You okay, honey?

794
00:52:09,835 --> 00:52:10,836
It's okay.

795
00:52:11,753 --> 00:52:13,130
M-Mom.

796
00:52:15,048 --> 00:52:17,843
My mom… is crying.

797
00:52:29,646 --> 00:52:32,149
DIRECTOR JANG'S LOCUM TENENS AGENCY

798
00:52:32,232 --> 00:52:35,402
LETTER OF RESIGNATION
GYE SU-JEONG

799
00:52:38,446 --> 00:52:42,617
The ex vivo multivisceral resection
and autotransplantation begins now.

800
00:52:42,701 --> 00:52:45,162
Our goal time is 15 hours.

801
00:52:45,245 --> 00:52:46,580
Let's be quick.

802
00:52:52,627 --> 00:52:53,712
SURGERY TIME

803
00:52:53,795 --> 00:52:55,922
CURRENT TIME

804
00:52:56,006 --> 00:52:57,757
MAGNOLIA BREAKFAST MEETING
MAY 3, 2026 08:00

805
00:52:59,843 --> 00:53:01,178
Wait, wait, what?

806
00:53:02,470 --> 00:53:03,471
How?

807
00:53:04,389 --> 00:53:07,142
How did… The IRB clearance
hasn't gone through yet!

808
00:53:07,225 --> 00:53:08,894
Guess she couldn't keep on waiting.

809
00:53:08,977 --> 00:53:11,146
The patient went critical this morning.

810
00:53:11,229 --> 00:53:13,815
Dr. Jo had the OR booked and ready
the whole time, apparently.

811
00:53:15,734 --> 00:53:18,904
<i>When a particular operation</i>
<i>is the only way forward,</i>

812
00:53:18,987 --> 00:53:22,073
hospital policy is to then
report it after the surgery,

813
00:53:22,157 --> 00:53:23,742
and call a meeting for discussion--

814
00:53:23,825 --> 00:53:25,202
Who else is operating?

815
00:53:26,203 --> 00:53:28,622
Jo Won-jin and Park Tae-gyeong.
They're both helping there.

816
00:53:30,207 --> 00:53:35,253
Does she intend to perform
that surgery entirely single-handed?

817
00:53:43,053 --> 00:53:45,764
Uh… So this is all a mass?

818
00:53:45,847 --> 00:53:47,641
AN ABNORMAL MASS
THAT HAS FORMED INSIDE THE BODY

819
00:54:01,821 --> 00:54:03,823
And now, we will all hear a few words

820
00:54:03,907 --> 00:54:07,285
from Chairman Kim Chang-su
of the Seonam Medical Association.

821
00:54:14,209 --> 00:54:16,336
VOTE ON A NATIONWIDE RESIDENTS' STRIKE
IN RESPONSE TO 2026 HEALTHCARE CRISIS

822
00:54:19,005 --> 00:54:21,925
Constantly throwing off
and putting on their lab coats again.

823
00:54:22,008 --> 00:54:23,593
These complaining kids.

824
00:54:23,677 --> 00:54:25,595
We are gathered here today

825
00:54:25,679 --> 00:54:30,016
to lay the foundation for a pivotal fight
that puts our white coats on the line.

826
00:54:33,436 --> 00:54:35,272
How much do you have left?

827
00:54:35,355 --> 00:54:37,941
I'm almost done. I just need
to get to one more vessel.

828
00:54:41,903 --> 00:54:42,904
SUNDAY, MAY 3

829
00:54:42,988 --> 00:54:44,698
We are holding this vote today

830
00:54:44,781 --> 00:54:48,493
to show that this approach of ours,
which follows a democratic process…

831
00:54:48,576 --> 00:54:50,245
The IVC clamp process.

832
00:54:50,328 --> 00:54:52,080
She's still not at that part, I bet.

833
00:54:53,206 --> 00:54:55,750
Well, who knows?
It's Gye Su-jeong, isn't it?

834
00:54:58,128 --> 00:54:59,629
That's true.

835
00:54:59,713 --> 00:55:01,923
Blocking flow to the IVC. Vascular clamp.

836
00:55:02,007 --> 00:55:04,092
A LARGE VEIN THAT SENDS BLOOD FROM
THE LOWER BODY AND ABDOMEN TO THE HEART

837
00:55:04,175 --> 00:55:06,594
- Heparin.
- Five-thousand units administered.

838
00:55:10,598 --> 00:55:13,268
And with that, we will now
begin the vote to determine

839
00:55:13,351 --> 00:55:15,478
whether we'll collectively resign.

840
00:55:15,562 --> 00:55:18,523
Before we proceed with that vote,
we've prepared a brief summary

841
00:55:18,606 --> 00:55:21,151
of the Korean Intern Resident
Association's current demands.

842
00:55:21,234 --> 00:55:22,068
SUNDAY, MAY 3

843
00:55:22,152 --> 00:55:23,778
Dr. Lee Mal-geum…

844
00:55:23,862 --> 00:55:27,032
She can handle it.
She'll do it on her own till then, right?

845
00:55:27,115 --> 00:55:29,034
It's Gye Su-jeong, isn't it?

846
00:55:29,993 --> 00:55:34,414
Even if she gets to the IVC, though,
the real challenge starts at that point.

847
00:55:35,582 --> 00:55:37,876
Oh, damn it. You're right.

848
00:55:38,460 --> 00:55:42,297
Hello. I'm Lee Mal-geum, a resident
in the Cardiothoracic Surgery Department.

849
00:55:44,049 --> 00:55:45,300
I'll try it through the shunt.

850
00:55:45,383 --> 00:55:46,885
A PASSAGE THAT CONNECTS BLOOD
OR OTHER BODILY FLUIDS

851
00:55:46,968 --> 00:55:48,428
TO FLOW THROUGH A DIFFERENT ROUTE

852
00:55:48,970 --> 00:55:50,597
You need to focus.

853
00:55:51,222 --> 00:55:52,223
Ah, right.

854
00:56:06,237 --> 00:56:08,198
<i>What we've been talking</i>
<i>about from the beginning,</i>

855
00:56:08,281 --> 00:56:10,450
<i>isn't simply a matter of numbers.</i>

856
00:56:11,117 --> 00:56:15,288
<i>We've been saying that the healthcare</i>
<i>system has long reached its limit.</i>

857
00:56:15,872 --> 00:56:19,209
<i>The government is seeing this situation</i>
<i>as a collective action or backlash to--</i>

858
00:56:19,292 --> 00:56:21,711
Ah! God damn it! I can't…

859
00:56:23,338 --> 00:56:25,006
Why is he standing up?

860
00:56:25,090 --> 00:56:26,674
GUSEO UNIVERSITY MEDICAL CENTER

861
00:56:28,134 --> 00:56:31,513
Who's that? Isn't that Dr. Do Yun-sik?

862
00:56:31,596 --> 00:56:33,473
Hey, what are you doing, Dr. Do?

863
00:56:33,556 --> 00:56:35,225
- Huh?
- You going to the bathroom?

864
00:56:35,308 --> 00:56:37,727
Uh, no. I… Oh, damn it.

865
00:56:37,811 --> 00:56:38,978
Don't tell me! No way!

866
00:56:40,563 --> 00:56:44,234
Oh, gosh, I… Bae Heung-gon,
watch the Director, please.

867
00:56:44,317 --> 00:56:45,902
Dr. Do!

868
00:56:45,985 --> 00:56:47,112
Yeah?

869
00:56:47,737 --> 00:56:49,864
Uh… I, uh…

870
00:56:52,158 --> 00:56:54,411
I can't keep holding it! Damn it!

871
00:56:54,494 --> 00:56:56,287
Ah!

872
00:56:59,958 --> 00:57:02,669
Are you okay?

873
00:57:12,011 --> 00:57:13,012
You're kidding me.

874
00:57:18,184 --> 00:57:19,644
This damn place!

875
00:57:22,856 --> 00:57:25,567
Oh, that little punk, I swear…
Now, where is she?

876
00:57:26,234 --> 00:57:27,694
I always knew that car'd break down,

877
00:57:27,777 --> 00:57:30,071
so I prayed we'd be safe and sound
when the time came.

878
00:57:30,155 --> 00:57:32,866
- I guess the prayer worked.
- She's not answering her phone.

879
00:57:32,949 --> 00:57:35,201
Still, why'd it break down then,
especially when we're in a hurry?

880
00:57:35,285 --> 00:57:36,536
I know.

881
00:57:36,619 --> 00:57:39,414
That little punk, that's it.
She'll pay for this.

882
00:57:40,915 --> 00:57:42,959
INPATIENT WARD, OUTPATIENT PHARMACY

883
00:57:43,042 --> 00:57:46,004
First, we demand
a scientific and open discussion…

884
00:57:46,087 --> 00:57:47,422
Where did Dr. Do go in a hurry?

885
00:57:48,840 --> 00:57:50,049
I'm not sure, it's a mystery to me.

886
00:57:50,133 --> 00:57:53,511
As this matter that will determine
the future of healthcare in Korea,

887
00:57:53,595 --> 00:57:57,056
a thorough discussion must
be had with experts in the field.

888
00:57:57,140 --> 00:57:58,141
SUNDAY, MAY 3

889
00:57:58,224 --> 00:57:59,893
If the government
truly cares about people,

890
00:57:59,976 --> 00:58:02,729
it will listen to the voices
of doctors and researchers.

891
00:58:02,812 --> 00:58:04,355
We demand a discussion.

892
00:58:09,152 --> 00:58:11,571
I-I-It's Do Yun-sik from General Surgery.

893
00:58:11,654 --> 00:58:12,780
Dr. Do!

894
00:58:12,864 --> 00:58:15,492
- Time out, time, time--
- Get in here already. Come assist.

895
00:58:16,534 --> 00:58:18,953
Okay, a shunt, get… get the shunt ready.

896
00:58:19,037 --> 00:58:21,831
- Huh? You already did it.
- Gosh, breathe, Dr. Do.

897
00:58:21,915 --> 00:58:23,291
Your hands are shaking.

898
00:58:23,374 --> 00:58:26,336
What? You only have one person assisting?

899
00:58:26,419 --> 00:58:28,421
Oh, God, this is crazy…

900
00:58:29,214 --> 00:58:31,716
Hey, but still, you're two steps ahead
of what I expected.

901
00:58:31,799 --> 00:58:34,260
I'm one step behind
where I was expecting to be.

902
00:58:34,344 --> 00:58:37,972
Yeah, as of today,
I'm gonna be right there with you.

903
00:58:38,056 --> 00:58:39,432
Satinsky clamp.

904
00:58:39,516 --> 00:58:40,391
A SURGICAL INSTRUMENT

905
00:58:40,475 --> 00:58:41,976
Clamping the celiac trunk.

906
00:58:50,610 --> 00:58:52,570
Come on, why is it taking so long?

907
00:58:56,199 --> 00:58:58,993
<i>Dr. Tae-wook to radiology, floor three.</i>

908
00:58:59,077 --> 00:59:02,163
<i>Dr. Tae-wook to radiology,</i>
<i>floor three. Thank you.</i>

909
00:59:05,500 --> 00:59:06,668
Hey!

910
00:59:08,336 --> 00:59:10,088
Booze?

911
00:59:11,381 --> 00:59:13,591
Are you crazy?
Is this what you went running back in for

912
00:59:13,675 --> 00:59:15,510
when you saw Su-jeong's resignation?
Really?

913
00:59:15,593 --> 00:59:18,054
What am I gonna do instead, huh?
You got an idea?

914
00:59:18,137 --> 00:59:21,391
And all that time and energy
it took you to get sober!

915
00:59:21,474 --> 00:59:22,767
Did you drink any?

916
00:59:22,850 --> 00:59:24,811
No, I haven't. Not a drop yet, I swear.

917
00:59:24,894 --> 00:59:25,979
Your hand.

918
00:59:26,563 --> 00:59:27,564
Your hand!

919
00:59:33,027 --> 00:59:34,404
You know this won't last long, right?

920
00:59:36,281 --> 00:59:37,907
It shouldn't be used too much, understand?

921
00:59:41,828 --> 00:59:43,830
Okay, let's go ahead.

922
00:59:43,913 --> 00:59:47,083
Su-jeong, that little brat,
she's really gonna get it from Auntie.

923
01:00:11,941 --> 01:00:13,151
Dissection is complete.

924
01:00:13,943 --> 01:00:16,738
Now… we take it out.

925
01:00:57,654 --> 01:01:01,532
We reiterate our demand
for a reasonable alternative.

926
01:01:01,616 --> 01:01:02,617
Thank you all.

927
01:01:07,455 --> 01:01:09,123
SUNDAY, MAY 3

928
01:01:16,214 --> 01:01:17,298
Well, Doctor?

929
01:01:18,132 --> 01:01:19,133
Yes?

930
01:01:19,217 --> 01:01:20,635
- Are you ready?
- Oh!

931
01:01:20,718 --> 01:01:21,969
Uh, yeah. Yes.

932
01:01:22,053 --> 01:01:23,429
Uh…

933
01:01:27,016 --> 01:01:30,728
Um… Yes, uh, thank you for your briefing,
Dr. Lee Mal-geum.

934
01:01:30,812 --> 01:01:33,690
Uh, okay, we will now proceed
with the vote.

935
01:01:33,773 --> 01:01:36,067
For collective submission
of letters of resignation,

936
01:01:36,150 --> 01:01:38,152
over 80 percent of votes
must be in favor of submitting.

937
01:01:49,122 --> 01:01:50,998
Connect to HTK.

938
01:01:51,082 --> 01:01:52,208
Starting the perfusion.

939
01:01:52,291 --> 01:01:54,502
PROCESS OF CIRCULATING BLOOD
THROUGH AN ORGAN OR TISSUE'S BLOOD VESSELS

940
01:02:01,968 --> 01:02:03,928
Gosh, now it really begins.

941
01:02:04,011 --> 01:02:06,639
It's really just us two doing this, right?

942
01:02:06,723 --> 01:02:08,057
- For real?
- We have to.

943
01:02:08,141 --> 01:02:10,643
God, this is so crazy…

944
01:02:10,727 --> 01:02:13,312
BP's 50 over 30. If it drops any lower…

945
01:02:13,396 --> 01:02:14,605
She'll suffer brain damage.

946
01:02:14,689 --> 01:02:16,315
I know that, kid.

947
01:02:16,399 --> 01:02:18,526
Someone…
Get someone else in here, quick. Okay?

948
01:02:18,609 --> 01:02:20,695
More assistants, whatever,
just get more people.

949
01:02:20,778 --> 01:02:22,530
We can't keep going like this.

950
01:02:22,613 --> 01:02:23,865
Hey, call somebody! I mean it!

951
01:02:23,948 --> 01:02:26,284
It doesn't matter who,
just get someone in here!

952
01:02:49,557 --> 01:02:51,601
General surgeon Jang Hui-suk.

953
01:02:54,437 --> 01:02:56,230
Uh, wait, wait, wait. What?

954
01:02:56,314 --> 01:02:58,107
Uh, who… W-Who…

955
01:02:58,191 --> 01:03:00,777
- Wait, no. Who the heck are you?
- Wait, Miss Jang?

956
01:03:00,860 --> 01:03:01,903
Miss Jang?

957
01:03:02,695 --> 01:03:04,197
Get a harmonic scalpel ready.

958
01:03:04,280 --> 01:03:06,324
Miss Jang? Jang, Jang Hu…

959
01:03:06,407 --> 01:03:08,785
What? You said you're a what?

960
01:03:09,619 --> 01:03:12,246
She is my teacher.

961
01:03:27,720 --> 01:03:30,681
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

962
01:04:09,804 --> 01:04:12,765
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

963
01:04:13,641 --> 01:04:16,978
I will make sure that
Hyeon-a grows up to be an adult.

964
01:04:17,061 --> 01:04:21,607
<i>If we are physicians,</i>
<i>then my question is, where do we belong?</i>

965
01:04:21,691 --> 01:04:23,067
<i>Stop the surgery!</i>

966
01:04:23,150 --> 01:04:25,444
<i>This surgery will be</i>
<i>carried through to completion.</i>

967
01:04:26,445 --> 01:04:29,407
You chose to do the surgery anyway,
thereby putting the patient in danger.

968
01:04:29,490 --> 01:04:32,034
With the staff being limited,
who will pick up the slack?

969
01:04:32,118 --> 01:04:35,162
<i>I assisted in the operation,</i>
<i>and I have no regrets about it.</i>

970
01:04:35,246 --> 01:04:38,666
<i>Gye Su-jeong! Contract terminated.</i>
